            <ArticleTitle>Facile silicification of plastic surface for bioassays.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2134-2137</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc09359k</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We herein report a biomimetic technique to modify plastic substrates for bioassays. The method first places a polydopamine adhesion layer to plastic surface, and then grows conformal silica coating. As proof of principle, we coated plastic microbeads to construct a disposable filter for point-of-care nucleic acid extraction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
